mia nguyen: quick ask — we're refactoring the SDK snippets used in the streaming + cursor pagination docs. want them to be tight, consistent across py/ts/go, and include an example for retry with exponential backoff + resume via cursor. can someone own a small pass? :wave:

alex belmont: I can take TS + Go. plan to mirror the python flow so semantics match. where are the current snippets?

mia nguyen: here's the doc PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/842 — snippets are inline under /guides/streaming-pagination.md. they currently show a naive reconnect (restart from beginning) which causes duplicate tokens for long streams.

samir patel: i'll update the docs PR for formatting (code fence language markers, short explanatory captions). also will add a tiny test harness for the py snippet so CI fails if it goes stale.

chris lee: important: retry should attempt to resume from last-acknowledged cursor, not restart. propose we add a small helper in each snippet: `resume_from_cursor(cursor, retry_policy)` that replays the request with the cursor param.

alex belmont: sketch for TS helper (will tidy before pushing):
```ts
async function fetchWithResume(url, cursor, retries = 3) {
  let attempt = 0;
  let backoff = 200;
  while (attempt < retries) {
    try {
      const res = await fetch(`${url}?cursor=${cursor}`);
      return await res.json();
    } catch (e) {
      attempt++;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff));
      backoff *= 2;
    }
  }
  throw new Error('max retries');
}
```

samir patel: nice. for python i'll mirror that pattern and add an inline note about idempotency and token dedupe.

mia nguyen: please also standardize variable names: use `cursor_token` everywhere (not `cursor` in some and `cursor_id` in others). small change but reduces confusion in code blocks.

chris lee: noted. also add a tiny comment about stream chunk boundaries: if you resume mid-chunk, the client should be able to detect partial token on the first message after resume and drop it if duplicate. a one-line sentence in the doc is enough.

alex belmont: i'll open a follow-up PR with TS/Go snippets and link the CI python snippet. will push branch `docs/snippet/stream-resume-compact` later today.

